an't just compare them directly because  these things aren't just areas they're  actually volumes so we've got the small  volume and then the large volume on the  outside so what we'll need is the  equation for the volume of a sphere  which you should remember from school  for over three hoops PI R cubed so now  we can just compare the ratio of the  little volume to the big volume so this  will be V little R against the bigger so  this is V little R this is the bigger  and we don't need to have the four over  three pi cuz they'll cancel out so all  we have here is 14  cubed divided by 46 cubed which equals  which equals zero point zero two eight  so if you multiply this by a hundred to  turn it into a percentage that's  actually like equals two point eight  percent so this is telling us that two  point eight percent of the galaxy is  within is not moving away from us faster  than light so that means one hundred  minus two point eight which is a is  roughly ninety seven percent so the  answer 97% of the galaxies in the  observable universe traveling away from  us faster than the speed of light quick  shout out to these people for giving it  a go and posting the answers in the  original video and yeah thanks for  watching let me know what you thought of  this video if it's a popular format I  might do some more all right bye
 

